The full orthogonal group, the stable subgroup and the arithmetic group of the moduli
space are three different objects, and only the last two act trivially on the discriminant
group. The docstring of `ActsTriviallyModTwo` now names all three, says which satisfies the
hypothesis, and records that the full group is transitive on primitive isotropic vectors —
so the separation is a statement about `Γ_Co`, not a statement about the lattice alone.

